{
  "_comment": [
    "The event emission policy (PGSS §6.9): Machine\\Generic\\Events holds",
    "one key per event-type segment, any of which may carry an Enabled",
    "REG_DWORD of 0 or 1; the deepest on a type's path decides, and the",
    "type's tier decides where none does. Essential types never consult it.",
    "",
    "  Events  Enabled = 1   Everything not switched off beneath is on,",
    "                        verbose and debug types included. Remove it",
    "                        (or set 0) to fall back to the tier defaults,",
    "                        standard on and verbose and debug off, for",
    "                        whatever the keys beneath do not decide.",
    "",
    "Every emitter reads the tree: the kernel (kmes/event_policy.c, a watch",
    "on this key, a change applied within about 50 ms plus one walk), and",
    "libpeios, peios-rs and libp-go for userspace components.",
    "",
    "Intended descriptor, NOT APPLIED by this seed. PGSS §6.9 asks for a",
    "SACL that audits writes, so that a change to what is recorded is",
    "itself recorded. The SACL wanted is",
    "",
    "    S:(AL;CI;0x10002;;;WD)",
    "",
    "a SYSTEM_ALARM ACE for Everyone, inherited by every key beneath, over",
    "KEY_SET_VALUE (0x2) | DELETE (0x10000): the continuous-audit mask a",
    "handle opened for writing then carries, so each write through it is",
    "recorded once registry write audit exists. Owner and DACL stay",
    "inherited from the Machine hive (Administrators and SYSTEM full,",
    "Authenticated Users read), which is what §6.9 asks for. The batch",
    "document reg apply reads has no field for a key's descriptor, so the",
    "SACL has to be set some other way until it gains one (for example",
    "`reg sd Machine\\Generic\\Events --set 'S:(AL;CI;0x10002;;;WD)' --sacl`",
    "as SYSTEM).",
    "",
    "Shipped by the kernel package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply. Until it is applied the key does",
    "not exist, every emitter decides by tier, and the kernel keeps its",
    "machine-root fallback watch armed to notice the key being created."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Events",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Enabled", "type": "dword", "data": 1 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
